and at the dithering of its policymakers. Why can't the Japanese government find the political will to fix the country's problems? Japan's Policy Trap offers a provocative new analysis of the country's protracted economic stagnation. Japanese insider Akio Mikuni and long-term Japan resident R. Taggart Murphy contend that the country has landed in a policy trap that defies easy solution. The authors, who have together spent decades at the heart of Japanese finance, expose the deep-rooted political arrangements that have distorted Japan's monetary policy in a deflationary direction. They link Japan's economic difficulties to the Achilles' heel of the U.S. economy: the U.S. trade and current accounts deficits. For the last twenty years, Japan's dollar-denominated trade surplus has outstripped official reserves and currency in circulation.","pageCount":314,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"Business & Economics","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-japan-s-policy-trap-akio-mikuni-and-r-taggart-murphy"}],"displaySummary":"The authors, who have together spent decades at the heart of Japanese finance, expose the deep-rooted political arrangements that have distorted Japan's monetary policy in a deflationary direction. They link Japan's economic difficulties to the Achilles' heel of the U.S. economy: the U.S. trade and current accounts deficits. For the last twenty years, Japan's dollar-denominated trade surplus has outstripped official reserves and currency in circulation.","primaryTopic":"Business, Capitalism & Corporations","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Business & Economics","confidence":"high","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Business & Economics","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Business & Economics","mappedSubject":"Business & Economics","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily analyzes Japan's economic policies and their st